  "notes": [
    "Own module of the maintainer (Jochen Walter). Source repository is rA1nm3n/showpace under integrations/companion (inspected commit 824fddf of 2026-11-09, read 2026-11-16); all provenance paths are relative to the root of that repository. The module does not live in the repo named in its manifest.",
    "The manifest.json and package.json repository field point to bitfocus/companion-module-showpace-timer. That repository does NOT exist: `gh api repos/bitfocus/companion-module-showpace-timer` answered HTTP 404 on 2026-11-16 (run locally by the maintainer). The module is therefore not published in the official Bitfocus module directory and cannot be installed from the Companion module store; it has to be loaded as a local development module from rA1nm3n/showpace (integrations/companion).",
    "Complete catalog: all 32 actions of ActionsSchema (src/actions.ts:6-39) and all 13 feedbacks of FeedbacksSchema (src/feedbacks.ts:8-23) are listed; every feedback is a boolean feedback (src/feedbacks.ts:141-279). Names, labels and descriptions are German, exactly as registered in the module source.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~2.1.3 (package.json): option values support expressions (derived from the 2.x base version, not set explicitly). Not tested against a running Companion instance.",
    "Control path: the module talks to the ShowPace server API (default port 4520, HTTP POST /api/v1/<command path>, status via WebSocket /ws) with an optional PIN sent as header X-Stagetimer-Pin (src/config.ts:3, src/client.ts:4 and 60, companion/HELP.md, docs/ARCHITEKTUR.md:125-131). The server also offers OSC on UDP 4521 (/stagetimer/<command path>), but the Companion module does not use it.",
    "Connection config fields (not part of the schema): host (default 127.0.0.1), port (default 4520, 1-65535, integer), pin (secret-text, optional) (src/config.ts:15-48).",
    "Toggle-style actions (timer_toggle, blackout, pres_black, pres_clicker, pres_overlay_timer, pres_monitor) with mode toggle flip the last state the module knows; without a known state the result is 'on' (src/commands.ts:49-52, 103-106). Presentation actions and feedbacks need the presentation hub of ShowPace; without it (HTTP 501) the actions log an error and the pres_* feedbacks stay inactive (companion/HELP.md).",
